read":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":2.6126858131542923,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":-0.779373221184866,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":0.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.18791821503222877,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":96.0,"_gate_pool_share":0.11354469280656465,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":85.4,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0010570824404450073,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":12.3,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.011229226727319408,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":64.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0273441263299741,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":54.4,"_gate_insider_own":0.00701,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":4.7,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"SSR Mining Inc., together with its subsidiaries, engages in the acquisition, exploration, and development of precious metal resource properties in the United States, T\u00fcrkiye, Canada, and Argentina. The company explores for gold dor\u00e9, copper, silver, lead, and zinc deposits. It holds interests in the \u00c7\u00f6pler located in Erzincan province, Turkey; the Marigold situated in Nevada, the United States; the Seabee located in Saskatchewan, Canada; and the Puna situated in Jujuy province, Argentina. The company was formerly known as Silver Standard Resources Inc. and changed its name to SSR Mining Inc. in August 2017. SSR Mining Inc. was incorporated in 1946 and is based in Denver, Colorado.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Rodney P. Antal Accountancy, B.Bus, C.P.A. | Executive Chairman | Age 58 | Compensation: $4.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $562K ranks in the below the sector median among Basic Materials peers. Each employee generates $83K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $15K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 8\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["SSR Mining Inc. is a mid-cap basic materials business with a $5.7B market cap on $1.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +12% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $242M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 15 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.19\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 32\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.1%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.2\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 107% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.065442484063944},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Basic Materials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Commodity price volatility and cost-curve position \u2014 in a downturn only the lowest-cost producer has a business, and the rest carry the overhead.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Environmental remediation liability \u2014 tightening regulations on emissions, tailings, and water use create open-ended balance-sheet risk that grows with each legislative cycle.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 19% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Valued at a 45% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Among the least levered in Basic Materials \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"(SSRM) and the Role of Price-Sensitive Allocations","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/91/SSRM_and_the_Role_of_Price-Sensitive_Allocations_110626070202_1793966522.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793966522.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"SSR Mining (SSRM) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/ssr-mining-ssrm-q3-20